Chapter: CatDrawSpec
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Geom
  cites Safari chapter Camera
  cites Safari chapter Paint
  cites Safari chapter Stills
  cites Safari chapter CatStills
  cites Safari chapter CatDraw
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 CatDraw: the cat's baked stills, placed at a screen anchor and lifted by the
 hop.

 THE LIFT IS THE ONE THING HERE THAT CRITTER DOES NOT HAVE, and it goes into the
 SAME scale as the art. `cat-pt` computes `b.y - (p.y + lift) * h`, so a lift of
 a tenth raises the cat by a tenth of its own pixel height rather than by a tenth
 of a pixel -- which is what makes the hop look the same size at every distance.
 Adding the lift after the multiply instead would give a leap that shrinks with
 range, and both forms agree at lift zero, so this is graded with a lift on.

 THE BUFFER IS 256 AND NOT CRITTER'S 512. Half the animal's, and a longer
 polygon is skipped rather than truncated -- the same refusal, a different
 number, and worth grading because the two chapters look alike enough to have
 their constants swapped.

 THE COMMAND COUNT IS GRADED AS A RELATIONSHIP, not against a number read off
 the baked table. A pose that draws emits exactly as many commands as the table
 has polygons for it; that holds whatever the baker last produced, where a
 written-down count would go stale the next time it ran. CatStillsSpec is what
 grades the table itself.

 We say:

Section: Placing A Point

 The anchor is the feet and the art scales by the pixel height, so a unit-frame
 half is half the cat's height across and up.

  feet : ScreenPt
  feet = ScreenPt { x = 100.0, y = 200.0 }

  pt-got : List Real
  pt-got =
    let a = cat-pt feet 50.0 0.0 (StillPt { x = 0.5, y = 0.4 })
    in let b = cat-pt feet 50.0 0.0 (StillPt { x = 0.0, y = 0.0 })
    in let c = cat-pt feet 50.0 0.0 (StillPt { x = -1.0, y = 1.0 })
    in [a.x, a.y, b.x, b.y, c.x, c.y]

  pt-want : List Real
  pt-want = [125.0, 180.0, 100.0, 200.0, 50.0, 150.0]

 THE LIFT SCALES WITH THE ART. A lift of a fifth raises every point by a fifth of
 the pixel height -- ten pixels at h = 50, twenty at h = 100 -- and leaves x
 alone. A lift added after the multiply would raise both by the same fifth of a
 pixel and this is where they part.

  lift-got : List Real
  lift-got =
    let a = cat-pt feet 50.0 0.2 (StillPt { x = 0.5, y = 0.4 })
    in let b = cat-pt feet 100.0 0.2 (StillPt { x = 0.5, y = 0.4 })
    in let z = cat-pt feet 50.0 0.0 (StillPt { x = 0.5, y = 0.4 })
    in [a.x, a.y, z.y - a.y, b.y, a.x - z.x]

  lift-want : List Real
  lift-want = [125.0, 170.0, 10.0, 140.0, 0.0]

 A whole polygon maps point by point, in order.

  pts-got : List Real
  pts-got =
    let ps = cat-pts feet 50.0 0.0 [StillPt { x = 0.0, y = 0.0 }, StillPt { x = 0.5, y = 0.4 }] 0
    in [ real-from-int (list-length ps),
         (list-at ps 0).x, (list-at ps 0).y, (list-at ps 1).x, (list-at ps 1).y ]

  pts-want : List Real
  pts-want = [2.0, 100.0, 200.0, 125.0, 180.0]

Section: The Buffer Guard

 Two hundred and fifty-six, and a longer polygon is dropped rather than
 shortened.

  many : Integer -> List StillPt
  many (n) = if n <= 0 then [] else [StillPt { x = 0.0, y = 0.0 }] & many (n - 1)

  poly-of : Integer -> StillPoly
  poly-of (n) = StillPoly { color = 9, grad = [], pts = many n }

  guard-got : List Integer
  guard-got =
    [ max-cat-pts,
      list-length (cat-poly feet 50.0 0.0 (poly-of 3)),
      list-length (cat-poly feet 50.0 0.0 (poly-of 256)),
      list-length (cat-poly feet 50.0 0.0 (poly-of 257)),
      list-length (cat-poly feet 50.0 0.0 (poly-of 2)) ]

  guard-want : List Integer
  guard-want = [256, 1, 1, 0, 0]

 It is a flat fill and it keeps its colour.

  solid-got : List Integer
  solid-got =
    let c = list-at (cat-poly feet 50.0 0.0 (poly-of 3)) 0
    in [c.tag, c.color, c.color2, list-length c.geom, list-length c.pts]

  solid-want : List Integer
  solid-want = [0, 9, 0, 0, 6]

 A list of polygons comes out in array order, which is the painter's order the
 baker preserved.

  polys-got : List Integer
  polys-got =
    [ list-length (cat-polys feet 50.0 0.0 [poly-of 3, poly-of 4, poly-of 300] 0),
      list-length (cat-polys feet 50.0 0.0 [] 0),
      list-length (list-at (cat-polys feet 50.0 0.0 [poly-of 3, poly-of 4] 0) 1).pts ]

  polys-want : List Integer
  polys-want = [2, 0, 8]

Section: Drawing One

 The pixel height is the projected gap between the feet and a point `height`
 metres above them, so a 1.7-metre cat through a focal of 500 is exactly one
 pixel at 850 metres -- the boundary, and it still draws.

  drawn : Real, Real -> Integer
  drawn (forward) (height) = list-length (cat-draw 0.0 forward height 0 0.0 500.0 960.0)

  size-got : List Integer
  size-got =
    [ drawn 850.0 1.7,
      drawn 851.0 1.7,
      drawn 2000.0 1.7 ]

  size-want : List Integer
  size-want = [list-length (cat-polys-for 0), 0, 0]

 A pose that draws emits one command per polygon the table holds for it, and the
 lift does not change how many.

  count-got : List Integer
  count-got =
    [ list-length (cat-draw 0.0 100.0 1.7 0 0.0 500.0 960.0),
      list-length (cat-draw 0.0 100.0 1.7 0 0.3 500.0 960.0),
      list-length (cat-draw 0.0 100.0 1.7 2 0.0 500.0 960.0) ]

  count-want : List Integer
  count-want =
    [ list-length (cat-polys-for 0),
      list-length (cat-polys-for 0),
      list-length (cat-polys-for 2) ]

 The table has art for every pose the state machine can name.

  table-got : List Boolean
  table-got =
    [ list-length (cat-polys-for 0) > 0,
      list-length (cat-polys-for 1) > 0,
      list-length (cat-polys-for 2) > 0,
      list-length (cat-polys-for 3) > 0,
      list-length (cat-polys-for 4) > 0,
      list-length (cat-polys-for 5) > 0,
      list-length (cat-polys-for 6) > 0 ]

  table-want : List Boolean
  table-want = [True, True, True, True, True, True, True]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "cd-pt    " pt-got pt-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "cd-lift  " lift-got lift-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "cd-pts   " pts-got pts-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "cd-guard " guard-got guard-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "cd-solid " solid-got solid-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "cd-polys " polys-got polys-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "cd-size  " size-got size-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "cd-count " count-got count-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "cd-table " table-got table-want)
  end
